Talent Corner - AI Microservice 🚀
This is the dedicated AI service for the Talent Corner Job Portal. It handles heavy computational tasks like resume parsing and job-match scoring using Python and Machine Learning.

🛠 Features
Resume Scorer: Analyzes PDF/DOCX resumes against job descriptions to provide a match percentage.

Text Extraction: Robust extraction of skills and experience from uploaded documents.

Scalable Architecture: Runs as an independent service to ensure the main Node.js backend remains fast.

📂 Project Structure
Plaintext
ai-server/
├── app.py              # Main Flask/FastAPI entry point
├── models/             # Pre-trained ML models or scoring logic
├── utils/              # PDF processing and text cleaners
├── .env                # API keys and configurations
└── requirements.txt    # Python dependencies
🚀 Getting Started
1. Prerequisites
Python 3.9 or higher

Pip (Python package manager)

2. Installation
Clone the repository:

Bash
git clone https://github.com/your-repo/ai-server.git
cd ai-server
Create a Virtual Environment:

Bash
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate  # On Windows: venv\Scripts\activate
Install Dependencies:

Bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
3. Running the Server
Bash
python app.py
The server will start on http://localhost:5000 (default).

📡 API Endpoints
POST /score
Takes a job description and a resume text to return a match score.

Request: {"job_description": "...", "resume_text": "..."}

Response: {"match_score": 85.5}

🤝 System Integration
This service is designed to communicate with the Talent Corner Node.js Backend. Ensure the VITE_AI_URL in your Frontend and the corresponding URL in your Backend are pointed to this service's address.

Final Step Before Pushing
Save this as README.md in your ai-server folder.

Crucial: Add a .gitignore to your AI repo so you don't push the venv/ folder!